{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception-action interface, separating sensing (uncontrollable) and motion (controllable) events. The specification enforces safe, coverage-biased exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are used only when obstacles are detected. Recovery is directed by left/right obstacle context, and full_rotate is reserved for rare deadlock cases. All transitions are deterministic and respect the runtime semantics.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for sensing and motion to reflect the DES architecture.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, deterministic, and coverage-oriented exploration with minimal recovery and no oscillation."
